&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50101662</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:26:04 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>How are you centralising AI for development at your company?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50101587</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I'm asking this because I'm seeing some frustrating patterns and if I may be bold, I think my answer is the correct one.&lt;p&gt;Here's one I'm seeing: its the SDLC agent pattern and I think its wrong.&lt;p&gt;Step 1: you have good AGENTS.md documentation for your code and other principles. (this is good)&lt;p&gt;Step 2: There's a somewhat strict workflow and steps enforced like planner agent, reviewer agent, critique agent and directly create a PR from a ticket. Every human intervention here is considered an anti-pattern.&lt;p&gt;I'd like it to be as simple as having documentation and giving developer full freedom with choice of harness, tools (MCP) and just make the pull request.&lt;p&gt;What's the logic behind the multi step planner, reviewer, critique agents?&lt;/p&gt;
